.TH "ET\-PARTYLINE\-SERVER" "1" "November 2026" ""
.SH NAME
et\-partyline\-server \- start a Partyline server for EmComm Tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]et\-partyline\-server\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]et\-partyline\-server\f[R] starts a Partyline server using the
Reticulum Network Stack (RNS).
.PP
A local Reticulum shared instance must already be running before
starting the Partyline server.
Use \f[B]et\-reticulum\f[R] to configure and start the shared instance.
.PP
The utility presents an interactive menu of available Partyline server
configuration blueprints.
The selected blueprint becomes the active server configuration.
.PP
Only one Partyline server instance may run at a time.
If a server is already running, the utility exits without starting
another.
.SH CONFIGURATION BLUEPRINTS
Unlike Reticulum blueprints, Partyline server blueprints are intended to
be customized by the operator.
EmComm Tools provides one sample configuration as a starting point:
.IP
.EX
\(ti/.config/partyline/config.blueprint.etc\-sample\-server.json
.EE
.PP
Available blueprints are discovered in \f[CR]\(ti/.config/partyline\f[R]
and presented in an interactive selection menu.
.PP
The selected blueprint is linked to \f[CR]server.json\f[R], replacing
the previous active configuration.
.PP
To create a custom blueprint, copy the sample configuration and save it
in \f[CR]\(ti/.config/partyline\f[R] as
\f[CR]config.blueprint.DESCRIPTIVE\-NAME\f[R].
Modify the configuration to meet your requirements.
Run \f[B]et\-partyline\-server\f[R] again to select the new blueprint.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
et\-partyline\-server
.EE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run \f[B]et\-partyline\-server\f[R] when starting a Partyline server or
switching to a different server configuration blueprint.
.PP
Ensure the Reticulum shared instance is running before starting the
server.
.PP
Stop any existing Partyline server instance before running this utility
again.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.config/partyline/config.blueprint.\f[R]*
Partyline server configuration blueprints offered in the selection menu.
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.config/partyline/server.json\f[R]
Symbolic link to the selected Partyline server configuration blueprint.
This file is replaced when another blueprint is selected.
